  <main id="main"><div class="container"><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow">From the notebook</p><h1>Good questions to keep asking</h1><p class="lead">A few questions that make opinions more useful, especially while they are still forming.</p><div class="meta"><span class="topic">Perspectives</span><time datetime="2026-10-08">8 October 2026</time><span>3 min read</span></div></header><div class="article-layout"><article class="prose"><p>An opinion is more helpful when you can see what shaped it. What problem was I trying to solve? What did I compare? How long did I spend with it? Who might have a very different result?</p>
<p>Those questions slow things down in a good way. They make room for a view that is specific and honest instead of pretending to be universal.</p>
<h2>Make space to change your mind</h2>
<p>Early impressions are worth recording, but they are not a final verdict. A follow-up after a month of use can be more revealing than a polished first look.</p>
<p>I hope this site can hold both: what seems true today and what turned out differently later.</p><a class="back-link" href="../../blog/">← Back to all notes</a></article><aside class="article-aside" aria-label="About this note"><p><strong>Perspectives</strong><br>8 October 2026<br>3 minute read</p><p>Have a thought about this note? <a href="../../contact/">Get in touch</a>.</p></aside></div></div></main>
